  "body": "For example, it could be quite convenient for crypto streams, as in https://gist.github.com/domenic/7337821.\n\nThe idea would be that you could do\n\n``` js\nwriteableStream.close().then(v => console.log(\"something useful?\", v));\n```\n\nor, if you weren't the one closing it,\n\n``` js\nwriteableStream.closed.then(v => console.log(\"something useful?\", v));\n```\n\nThe alternative is to say that writable streams should add their own properties, like the `.hash` property in the above gist, for such cases. This might be conceptually cleaner, since it's not like the idea of a \"close value\" has general applicability to the writable stream concept.\n",
